---
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---

<Specimen
  title="A lesson's trail"
  code={`<Breadcrumbs items={[
  { label: 'Systems', href: '/systems' },
  { label: 'ZX Spectrum', href: '/systems/sinclair-zx-spectrum' },
  { label: 'Sinclair BASIC', href: '/systems/sinclair-zx-spectrum/basic' },
  { label: 'Meet BASIC', href: '/systems/sinclair-zx-spectrum/basic/meet-basic' },
  { label: 'Make the Spectrum answer' },
]} />`}
  note="A nav named Breadcrumb holding an ordered list; the last item, the current page, carries aria-current='page' and is not a link. Interface, so nothing is filled or framed (§7), and set in the interface face (§4). The current page is drawn in the full ink rather than inverse video: the site's nav already shows it in inverse, and the page's own heading follows the trail (§7). The separators are drawn rules, hidden from screen readers. At phone width the trail wraps."
  block
>
  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[
      { label: 'Systems', href: '#' },
      { label: 'ZX Spectrum', href: '#' },
      { label: 'Sinclair BASIC', href: '#' },
      { label: 'Meet BASIC', href: '#' },
      { label: 'Make the Spectrum answer' },
    ]}
  />
</Specimen>

<Specimen
  title="Short, with the current page still linked"
  code={`<Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Vault', href: '/vault' }, { label: 'People', href: '/vault/people' }]} />`}
  note="Give the last item an href only if it should stay a link; it then carries aria-current itself."
  block
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Vault', href: '#' }, { label: 'People', href: '#people' }]} label="Breadcrumb, linked" />
</Specimen>
